      "role": "user",
      "content": "rebuild what though? there's nothing left to build on. i'm 45. i dont have the energy to start from scratch again. it feels like i've been running a marathon for 20 years only to find out the finish line was a cliff. honestly, it feels more logical to just stop than to keep trying to find meaning in a life that's clearly already been spent. it's like a bad investment you just have to walk away from.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
